{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The expression to differentiate includes an exponential term.\n\nRemember that the derivative of the general exponential term $a^x$ (where $a$ is any positive constant) is $\\ln(a)\\cdot a^x$.\n\nPut another way, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}(a^x)=\\ln(a)\\cdot a^x$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d}{dx}(-3\\cdot10^x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-3\\dfrac{d}{dx}(10^x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-3\\cdot\\ln(10)\\cdot10^x\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}(-3\\cdot10^x)=-3\\ln(10)\\cdot10^x$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Find $\\dfrac{d}{dx}(-3\\cdot10^x)$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$-3\\ln(10)\\cdot 10^x$","correct":true},{"content":"$-3\\ln(x)\\cdot 10^x$","correct":false},{"content":"$-3\\log(x)\\cdot 10^x$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$-3\\cdot 10^{x}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
